course: dictionary
lesson: 7060
title: Patchwork: many parts joined together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Patchwork means many different pieces joined together to make one whole thing. In sewing, small pieces of different cloth are stitched together to make a quilt, cushion or bag.
explain: The word can also describe a mixture of different parts. In «"be" (am, is, was, were) is built the same patchwork way», the clue is that the forms come from different old words, so patchwork means mixed together from many sources. Check it by swapping in "mixed together": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look for context clues. Words like «built», «pieces» and «mixture» tell you that patchwork is about joining different things. If you can picture the sewing or the mix, you have found the meaning.
fact: Patchwork is a sewing craft where small pieces of different cloth are stitched together.
fact: Patchwork can be a noun (a patchwork quilt) or an adjective (a patchwork of fields).
fact: A patchwork of things is a mixture of many different parts, such as fields of different colours seen from above.
fact: «"Went" was once the past of an old verb "wend", meaning to go.»
fact: When a verb's forms come from different words, it is called suppletion, and «"be" (am, is, was, were)» is built the same patchwork way.
exercise: Which of these is a patchwork? | *A quilt made from many small pieces of cloth stitched together | A tin of paint | A single plain sheet of one colour | A pair of muddy boots
exercise: Ravi says a patchwork of fields means one big empty field. Is he right? | Yes, and it is always wet | *No, it means many different fields, like parts of different colours | No, it means a flat road | Yes, one big empty field
exercise: In «a patchwork quilt», what kind of word is patchwork? | Noun | Verb | Pronoun | *Adjective
test: What does «a patchwork of rules» mean? | One rule only | *A mixture of many different rules | A rule written on cloth | A rule that is forgotten
test: Which sentence shows patchwork as sewing? | He ran to school before lunch. | The sky was blue all day. | Water boils at one hundred degrees. | *She stitched small squares of cloth into a patchwork cushion.
exam: Why is «be» described as patchwork in the lesson? | It has only one letter | *Its forms come from different old words | It is a sewing word | Its spelling never changes
